So a quoted structured value like `JSCOMPS="a;b;c"` - inside quotes, ';' is just a regular char (default case PUTC). So the buffer accumulates "a;b;c". Then when closing quote, returns 0. Then back in _parse_param_value case '"', after the while loop, r==0, break. Then continues the outer while. Next char... eventually ':' or ';' ends it, calling set_value_from_string with "a;b;c".

